\begin{enumerate}
    \item Multiply both sides by $x-1$:
    \[3x+2 = 4(x-1)\]
    \item Distribute the 4:
    \[3x+2 = 4x-4\]
    \item Subtract $3x$ from both sides:
    \[2 = x-4\]
    \item Add 4 to both sides:
    \[6 = x\]
\end{enumerate}
So, $x = 6$.

