\textbf{Solution:}
Let $V$ be the volume of the cube and $s$ be the side length of the cube.
The volume of a cube is given by $V = s^3$.
We are given that $V = 0.027$ cubic meters.
Thus, we have $s^3 = 0.027$.
Taking the cube root of both sides, we get $s = \sqrt[3]{0.027} = 0.3$ meters.
The surface area of a cube is given by $A = 6s^2$.
Substituting $s = 0.3$ into the formula, we get $A = 6(0.3)^2 = 6(0.09) = 0.54$ square meters.

\boxed{0.54 \text{ square meters}}
\boxed{0.54}

