\begin{enumerate}
    \item Original volume of the cube:
    The original cube has side length $s = 2$ cm. Therefore, the volume of the cube is $V = s^3 = 2^3 = 8$ cubic centimeters.
    \item New volume:
    The new volume is the original volume increased by 19 cubic centimeters, so the new volume is $V_{\text{new}} = 8 + 19 = 27$ cubic centimeters.
    \item Side length of the new cube:
    Let $s_{\text{new}}$ be the side length of the new cube. Then $V_{\text{new}} = s_{\text{new}}^3$. We have $27 = s_{\text{new}}^3$, so $s_{\text{new}} = \sqrt[3]{27} = 3$ centimeters.
\end{enumerate}
\boxed{3} 
